description:
Responsibilities
- Assist sales team to complete regional project sales tasks;
- For specific projects, complete the requirements collection, solution design & presentation, on-site testing and training;
- Work with BDM local teams to develop industry market customers, explore project opportunities, follow up project progress and promote project landing;
- Promotion, training and technical guidance for industry-based products and solutions to internal sales and DPP customers;
- According to industry market demand collection and research, combined with competitor program analysis, develop regional industry solutions;
- Cooperate with salesmen, organize preparation and implementation of product-related promotion conferences, exhibitions, customer visits, etc.
Qualifications
- Bachelor degree or above, major in computer, communication, electronics, IT etc;
- At least 2 years experience in the security industry, pre-sales & project support experience
- Familiar with video surveillance products and related solutions, systematically understand network, storage, server, etc., can independently configure technical proposals, design technical solutions
- In possession with successful experience focused on Safe City & Intelligent Transportation solutions;
- Industry market research and analysis, competitor analysis experience, and promotion of industry product solutions;
- Good communication skills and persuasiveness, independent analytical and problem solving skills;
- Fluent English and Arabic both in reading, writing and speaking

Qualifications
1. Bachelor's degree or above, in Quality Management, Industrial Engineering, Mechanical Manufacturing, or related fields;
2. More than 2 years of experience in Quality Management Systems, with ISO9001 Internal Auditor certification;
3. Familiarity with ISO9001 Quality Management System standards and requirements;
4. Experience in establishing and maintaining Quality Management Systems;
5. Proficiency in Quality Management tools and methods;
6. Strong analytical and organizational coordination skills;
7. Good written communication and training skills;
8. Rigorous and meticulous work style, with a strong sense of responsibility.
9. Candidates with ISO9001 auditor certificate are preferred.
Job Responsibilities
1. Establishment of Quality Management System: Establish and maintain the company's quality management system to ensure compliance with ISO9001 and other standards;
2. System Document Management: Prepare, revise, and maintain quality management system documents, including quality manuals, procedure documents, work instructions, etc.;
3. Internal Audit Management: Organize and implement internal quality audits, track the rectification of issues identified during audits;
4. Management Review Support: Assist in organizing management review meetings, track the implementation of review decisions;
5. Quality Objective Management: Set the company's quality objectives, monitor the achievement of these objectives, and analyze the reasons for any deviations;
6. Continuous Improvement Promotion: Drive the continuous improvement of the quality management system, enhancing quality management levels;
7. Quality Training Management: Organize quality management training to improve employee quality awareness and skills;
8. Customer Audit Response: Assist in responding to customer quality audits, prepare audit materials, and track the rectification of audit issues.
9. Product Certification: Responsible for the company’s product SASO certification, including product testing, handling test issues, and interfacing with certification bodies;
